# trembita documentation

## No reference projects

Do **not** name, link, or allude to external product apps, customer codebases, or private reference implementations in trembita documentation.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
Quazala's gateway port proved that most routes are data.
Real product apps serve as migration targets.
export TREMBITA_STATIC_ADMIN_BUCKET=quazala-fe-admin

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
Large route tables (100+ routes) are mostly declarative data.
Validate conventions via examples/ and integration tests in this repo.
export TREMBITA_STATIC_ADMIN_BUCKET=my-app-fe-admin
```

Use only **in-repo** illustrations:

- `examples/` and `showcase/`
- crate APIs, tests, and scripts under this workspace
- generic placeholders (`my-app`, `api.example.com`, `my-app-fe-admin`)

Decision records describe trembita design and migration paths — not third-party adoption timelines or parity scripts living outside the repo.
